meta {
  name: Cron endpoint requires auth
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/cron/renewal-warnings
  headers {
    Authorization: Bearer wrong-secret
  }
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 403
}

settings {
  followRedirects: false
}

docs {
  Cron routes are exempt from the page-level session redirect (Vercel Cron
  carries `Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}` but no session cookie — the
  old redirect silently bounced the daily job to /login). The handler gates
  itself: a wrong/absent bearer returns 403 when CRON_SECRET is set in the
  app's env. NOTE: this assertion requires the running app to have CRON_SECRET
  set; with it unset the route has no secret to check and this test does not
  apply (see bruno/README.md and Local.bru).
}
